# rcm configuration
# Symlinked to ~/.rcrc
# See rcrc(5) for full documentation

# Dotfiles location
DOTFILES_DIRS="$HOME/workspace/dotfiles"

# Files/directories to NEVER symlink
# These are docs, scripts, support files, or managed separately
#
# Note: Platform-specific configs use the tag system:
#   - tag-macos/  → only symlinked when TAGS includes "macos"
#   - tag-linux/  → only symlinked when TAGS includes "linux"
#   - tag-server/ → only symlinked when TAGS includes "server"
#
# Examples:
#   - config/karabiner is in tag-macos/, so Linux won't get it
#
# ml4w-managed configs (sourced/hooked, not symlinked):
#   - config/hypr - ml4w manages ~/.config/hypr, custom.conf sources our files
#
# config/kitty is NOT excluded here. It used to be, which meant NO machine ever
# got a kitty config - including macOS, where ml4w does not exist. kitty then
# fell back to its default font and every Nerd Font glyph in the prompt and in
# eza's icons rendered as a box. The exclusion is ml4w-specific, so it belongs
# in ~/.rcrc.local where the ml4w flag is handled, not in this base config.
# Name files exactly here and never use a wildcard. A bare name matches at any
# depth, so a ./ prefix is what limits a name to the repo root. rcm also expands
# a pattern such as *.md against the folder it is reading, which dropped
# claude/CLAUDE.md with no message and left no way to include it again. A file
# that is not named here gets linked, which is visible, and
# scripts/check-rcm-links.sh checks the rest.
EXCLUDES="README.md ./CLAUDE.md ./AGENTS.md .git .gitignore .gitmodules .brew .cask .osx docs packages hooks setup_mac.sh setup_ubuntu.sh brew prompt ls ssh sublime termux tridactyl vim zsh tmux git mise.toml ml4w config/hypr rcrc.local .rcm-not-linked"

# rcrc.local is machine state that install.sh writes, never a file to link.
# A stray copy inside a repo would otherwise be linked over the real one.

# Claude Code skills are folders, and each one is linked whole.
SYMLINK_DIRS="claude/skills/*"

# Source machine-specific rcrc settings (tags, hostname)
# Create ~/.rcrc.local with:
#   TAGS="desktop macos"
#   HOSTNAME="your-hostname"
[[ -f ~/.rcrc.local ]] && source ~/.rcrc.local
